data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":88,"item_id":"rs_045e2390a8206182016ac9666752f08193b449bb01ab9261fe","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering file management**\n\nI’m pondering whether I have enough time to test a new file reuse helper. I need to figure out if I can append to an existing file while ensuring that I’m not duplicating content. Would it be better to have standalone helpers, or can I just modify the last block for a larger file? I want to avoid redundancy and maintain unique last lines, but I’m not entirely sure of the best approach yet."}

